  {
    "name": "fetch_url",
    "description": "Direct HTTP fetch — raw bytes only, no JS rendering, no browser. Uses the\nshared undici keep-alive pool (SubprocessManager.acquireHttpClient) and the\nsame SSRF guard as browse_headless.\n\nUse for:\n  - raw HTML source (unlike browse_headless which gives rendered DOM)\n  - JSON REST API responses (returns JSON verbatim)\n  - plain text / CSV / XML / static assets\n  - latency- or token-sensitive fetches (4x faster + 4x cheaper than browse)\n\n[Prefer browse_headless for]:   JS-heavy SPAs (fetch won't run scripts).\n[Prefer browse_headless for]:   structured a11y snapshot (Playwright-style).\n[Prefer browse_headless for]:   anti-bot sites (Cloudflare blocks raw fetch).\n[Prefer browse_logged_in for]:  authenticated endpoints (fetch_url sends no cookies).\n[Prefer screenshot for]:        a rendered image of the page.\n[Prefer pdf for]:               a paginated PDF of the page.\n[Prefer network for]:           the page's resource load trace.\n\nDOES NOT:\n  - follow redirects (3xx → outcome=didnt + data.location; re-call fetch_url\n    on the new URL yourself — keeps SSRF caller-explicit per hop)\n  - execute JavaScript or render pages\n  - send cookies / Authorization (set options.headers explicitly if needed)\n  - retry on failure (caller-tier decision, not engine decision)\n  - fall back to browse_headless (INV-23 honored: fetch vs browse never fall back)\n\nBODY ROUTING by Content-Type (parse6 §3.5):\n  text/html, application/xhtml+xml         → body_kind=html (raw text)\n  application/json, */+json                → body_kind=json (raw text)\n  text/plain, text/css, text/csv, text/xml → body_kind=text (raw text)\n  image/*, video/*, application/pdf, etc.  → body_kind=binary:<subtype>\n                                            (base64-encoded text)\n\nEXTRACT MODE (v1.1) — options.extract_mode transforms HTML bodies post-fetch:\n  omit / 'raw'           DEFAULT. Raw HTML bytes verbatim (v1.0 byte-identical).\n                         Non-HTML routes (json/text/binary) IGNORE this field.\n  'markdown'             HTML only: defuddle strips nav/ads → turndown to clean markdown.\n                         body_kind becomes 'markdown:<engine>'. Saves tokens for LLM input.\n  'markdown_cited'       markdown + ⟨N⟩ citation footnotes + References section (RAG).\n\nSECURITY: URL is SSRF-checked. Private IPs (10.x / 127.x / 169.254.169.254\nmetadata / 192.168.x) blocked; default allowlist passes 198.18.0.0/15 (fake-ip\nTUN) + 127.0.0.1/32 (CDP). Extend via LASSO_SSRF_ALLOW_RANGES='cidr1,cidr2'.\nredirect:'manual' ensures redirects cannot be used to bypass SSRF.\n\nBOUND: response > 48 KiB auto-spills to /tmp/lasso-output/@oN.txt (mode 0o600)\nand the response carries a 16 KiB preview + ref — read_text({ref:@oN, offset}).\n\nArgs:  url (str, required)               — http(s) URL (userinfo @ forbidden)\n       options.method (str, default 'GET')  — 'GET' | 'HEAD' (POST/PUT not in v0.5)\n       options.headers (object, optional)   — custom request headers\n       options.timeout_ms (int, default 30000, max 60000)\n       options.max_bytes (int, default 2097152, max 16777216)  — 2 MiB default, 16 MiB cap\n       options.no_cache (bool, default false)  — adds Cache-Control: no-cache\n       options.extract_mode (str, optional)  — 'raw' | 'markdown' | 'markdown_cited' (HTML only; v1.1)\n\nReturns: InteractResult<FetchUrlResult> as JSON text.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "url": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uri"
        },
        "options": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "method": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "GET",
                "HEAD"
              ],
              "default": "GET"
            },
            "headers": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "timeout_ms": {
              "type": "integer",
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
              "maximum": 60000,
              "default": 30000
            },
            "max_bytes": {
              "type": "integer",
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
              "maximum": 16777216,
              "default": 2097152
            },
            "no_cache": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "default": false
            },
            "extract_mode": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "raw",
                "markdown",
                "markdown_cited"
              ]
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "default": {}
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "url"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
    },
