  {
    "name": "network",
    "description": "Capture the network resource list of a URL via JS-level PerformanceObserver\ninjection (navigates first, then injects an observer for options.timeout_ms ms,\nthen resolves the resource entries). Returns a JSON list of resources + a\nthird-party count, auto-spilling to /tmp/lasso-output/@oN (mode 0o600) when it\nexceeds 48 KiB; read the spill file with read_text({ref:@oN, offset}).\n\nUse for:\n  - auditing third-party trackers / analytics / ad networks on a page\n  - debugging slow page loads (TTFB / duration per resource)\n  - seeing what XHR/fetch the page makes (filter: 'xhr' or 'fetch')\n  - estimating page weight (sum of transferSize across resources)\n\n[Prefer browse_headless for]:  full DOM + a11y tree (network is one slice).\n[Prefer fetch_url for]:        raw HTML/JSON bytes of the main document only.\n[Prefer screenshot for]:       a visual snapshot (not a network list).\n[Prefer pdf for]:              a printable archive (not a network list).\n\nGO/NO-GO F2 (parse6 §4.4 + §7.1): PerformanceObserver is a JS-level API, so it\ncaptures only resources the browser fetched after JS started. Under SSRF-\nallowlisted fake-ip / TUN proxies (Surge, Clash) the proxy may rewrite DNS or\ntiming, so some entries can be missed or have skewed metrics. When this is\ndetected the response includes data.next_step recommending CDP Network-level\ncapture (planned for v0.7 F3.7.x).\n\nDOES NOT:\n  - capture CDP Network-level requests (JS-level only; v0.7+ for full HAR)\n  - capture WebSocket frames (v1.0+)\n  - capture response bodies in v0.5 (options.include_bodies accepted for\n    forward-compat but not wired; POST v0.6)\n  - mock / intercept / replay requests (永远 NO-GO; v1.0+)\n  - export a HAR file (v0.7 F3.7.x)\n  - accept pageRef @pN in v0.5 (only URL; pageRef arrives in v0.6 forest merge)\n  - fall back across surfaces (INV-23 honored)\n\nHINT: performance entries may be incomplete under proxy/TUN — if the count\nlooks low for a heavy page, retry with options.timeout_ms=10000 or use the\ndata.next_step hint.\n\nArgs:  url (str, required)             — http(s) URL (userinfo @ forbidden)\n       options.filter (str, default 'all') — 'xhr' | 'fetch' | 'img' | '3rd-party' | 'all'\n       options.include_bodies (bool, default false) — v0.5: accepted, not wired (v0.6)\n       options.timeout_ms (int, default 3000) — PerformanceObserver采集窗口 (max 30000)\n       options.wait_until (str, default 'load') — 'load' | 'domcontentloaded' | 'networkidle'\n\nReturns: InteractResult<NetworkResult> as JSON text.\n        data.envelope carries preview (first 16 KiB of resource list JSON) + ref when spilled.\n        data.resource_count + data.third_party_count are always present on outcome=worked.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "url": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uri"
        },
        "options": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "filter": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "xhr",
                "fetch",
                "img",
                "3rd-party",
                "all"
              ],
              "default": "all"
            },
            "include_bodies": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "default": false
            },
            "timeout_ms": {
              "type": "integer",
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
              "maximum": 30000,
              "default": 3000
            },
            "wait_until": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "load",
                "domcontentloaded",
                "networkidle"
              ],
              "default": "load"
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "default": {}
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "url"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
